==Evolution==
Evolves into '''God Dragon Kamukura''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God Emperor Kamukura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kamukura is an effective, though very expensive, [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red unit]]. However, he is mostly rendered useless without support thanks to his attack rate.

The knockback and slow effect is especially useful against Red pushers, such as [[Bore]], [[Shy Boy]] and [[J.K. Bun Bun]].

Before True Form, Kamukura has underwhelming stats and a sluggish attack rate combined with high cost that prevent him from being an ideal generalist.

==='''True Form'''===
God-Emperor Kamukura receives better health, range and attack rate. These improvements aim at making him a better generalist, now able to outrange [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]]. However, he doesn't receive any new abilities or better uptime, and as a result, his performance against Red enemies doesn't change. Overall, not a groundbreaking [[True Form]], but a solid one regardless.

==='''Talents'''===
Among Kamukura's Talents, [[Resistant]] is the most notable. At level 30, his effective HP against Red enemies is 425k. Since Kamukura has way too much range for a Tanker, this Talent only serves to better his defense against Reds. This is good in that it allows him to tank hits from dangerous enemies like [[Professor A.]] and [[Berserkory]], but, beyond that, it does very little. Kamukura's cooldown is also too long to be safely used as a Tanker.

[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] allows him to be useful in [[Uncanny Legends]], though Kamukura already has enough range to avoid getting Cursed. Slow Resist, on the other hand, only affects his usage against [[Professor A.]], not worth the investment beyond such.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
While one might assume that [[Sage Slayer]] would unlock an entirely new niche for Kamukura to take advantage of, there are very few Red/Sage enemies in the game. Even with that, it can benefit you on occasion to Slow down [[Doctor K.O.]]'s movement, as he is a notoriously aggressive pusher. Regardless, it is not recommended to unlock this Ultra Talent for that reason alone.

Cost Down addresses one of Kamukura's most prominent issues: his outrageously high cost—with which he would hardly ever be worth sending out over other, cheaper, more cost-efficient Red crowd-controllers. This Ultra Talent brings Kamukura down to the standard price range of ''~4,500¢'' for [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Super Rare Cats]]. Although useful for people already investing in Kamukura, this Ultra Talent should not be the reason why you get him to level 60.

Kamukura's most important Ultra Talent is the increasing of his Slow activation rate from 50% to 100%. Now, Kamukura can be a reliable crowd-controller for his target trait and will have an overall Slow uptime approaching 75%. This Ultra Talent is well worth the investment for those interested in using Kamukura.

Overall, Kamukura's Ultra Talents are passable for those willing to invest in him, but they offer no incentive to reach that point if you are already satisfied with your current anti-Red firepower.

