==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Kamukura was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Dragon Emperors (Removed Combo)|Dragon Emperors]].
*Kamukura's tail resembles the [[wikipedia:Seven-Branched Sword|Seven-Branched Sword]].
*This Cat is a reference to the Dragon [[wikia:dragonball:Shenron|Shenron]] from ''Dragon Ball''. Its strength against Red enemies could be a reference to the [[wikia:dragonball:Red Ribbon Army|Red Ribbon Army]]. Even its description of its Evolved Form references the "7 [dragon] balls" collected, causing him to shift to his True Form. This is a blatant reference to how the 7 dragon balls work.
**In Evolved and True Form, a One-Star Orb and 2 Three-Stars Orbs confirmed that these orbs belong to the 7 Dragon Balls.
*This cat also has a distinct reference to the ancient sea creature named the Leviathan, or more specifically the Final Fantasy interpretation of it. Leviathan in the aforementioned series is generally the strongest Water elemental attack available in game and, usually, one of the strongest Summons. Speaking of which, the appearance also closely resembles a colorless version of the Water Dragon from Final Fantasy VI. Its attack, summoning a geyser of water, may also refer to the dragon's habitat as many Lung dragons are seen having relation to rivers. In fact, there are legends which imply that the Yellow River was once a dragon.

